  "findings": "Inspected the Wildlife Trusts spring shoot photograph and compared all three size pilots and 36 variants. Opposite broad lanceolate leaf pairs follow upright stems with an open clonal tuft silhouette rather than a green sphere; current variants span 0.20-0.38 m. No invented bright flower heads or summer fruit. Small green florets and toothed margins cannot individually resolve at 25 mm; top stem tips are their coarse representation. Accepted as stylized spring dogs mercury foliage, with source approval separate from user endorsement.",
